{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1219522-swimming-and-underwater-rules","id":1219522,"title":"Swimming and underwater rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-16T20:38:34-07:00","id":1219522,"title":"Swimming and underwater rules","content":"Quick question: does anyone know if there are swimming/underwater rules in the core? I swear I remember them being in there and can\u2019t find them. I might be thinking of another edition. I found the drowning rules but that\u2019s it. Anything else in there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T00:04:52-07:00","id":1219547,"title":"","content":"Unless I'm mistaken swimming is covered by athletics and the drowning/holding breathe rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T04:41:28-07:00","id":1219575,"title":"","content":"Yes. That and any <i>situational penalties</i> the story teller feels appropriate are basically it.<br /> <br /> Well, there is, sort of, a mention in the Difficult Terrain rules on page 199. And the Boyant tag for armors notes that, <i>without it</i>, \u200bMobility Penalties will apply to swimming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T05:52:06-07:00","id":1219595,"title":"","content":"I miss Second Edition\u2019s explicit rules that being underwater imposed a general penalty to actions by characters who are not built to exist underwater. Including a penalty to using projectile weapons. <br /> <br /> One of the few marks against Third Edition is treating the matter like the Air-Breathing Mermaid Problem. The problem (Mermaids can\u2019t breathe air) isn\u2019t addressed in the rules, only revealed in the special abilities that let you ignore those rules. <br /> <br /> Likewise, fatigue penalties. There should have been a few sentences as a guideline for why and when characters suffer from it. Though I\u2019m fine with not having a mathematical calculation as I think Second Edition had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T05:55:32-07:00","id":1219597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1219522-swimming-and-underwater-rules?p=1219595#post1219595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I miss Second Edition\u2019s explicit rules that being underwater imposed a general penalty to actions by characters who are not built to exist underwater. Including a penalty to using projectile weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the ST is for.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of levels of penalty an ST could decide to levy against a PC performing underwater actions, from &quot;no penalty&quot; to &quot;-2 dice&quot; to &quot;you straight-up can't do this thing,&quot; with the level at least partially set by how much the ST cares about real-world physics versus high action movie logic. Setting it in stone makes the choice <i>for</i> you, and I'd prefer to leave it to the ST's judgment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-17-2018, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T08:55:10-07:00","id":1219667,"title":"","content":"There was a whole section of Athletics charms about being in the water in the playtest at one point. They all got cut. But at one point they existed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T09:04:41-07:00","id":1219669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1219522-swimming-and-underwater-rules?p=1219667#post1219667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a whole section of Athletics charms about being in the water in the playtest at one point. They all got cut. But at one point they existed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was actually part of the playtest so I may be remembering this. That would make a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T11:41:21-07:00","id":1219730,"title":"","content":"Mobility Penalties apply to all actions underwater too. Just so you know!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T21:08:15-07:00","id":1219875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Therian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1219522-swimming-and-underwater-rules?p=1219669#post1219669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually part of the playtest so I may be remembering this. That would make a lot of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how odd I\u2019ve found the utter lack of printed swimming Charms (even DBs only have one despite Water Aspects being a thing!), the idea that there were but they got chosen for the chopping block perplexes me even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T23:55:58-07:00","id":1219890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1219522-swimming-and-underwater-rules?p=1219875#post1219875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering how odd I\u2019ve found the utter lack of printed swimming Charms (even DBs only have one despite Water Aspects being a thing!), the idea that there were but they got chosen for the chopping block perplexes me even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that for the sake of streamlining charm lists the decision was made to let athletics charms and environmental effect rules suffice for swimming while &quot;giving&quot; storytellers the latitude to adjudicate the grey areas. <br /> <br /> I'm not an Ex3 ST but I can see treating swimming as using all athletics charms and athletics with situational modifiers for land-natives as well as drowning rules. Throw in the odd sail charm and Robert is your father's brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T00:44:27-07:00","id":1219895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1219522-swimming-and-underwater-rules?p=1219875#post1219875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how odd I\u2019ve found the utter lack of printed swimming Charms (even DBs only have one despite Water Aspects being a thing!), the idea that there were but they got chosen for the chopping block perplexes me even more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least Dragonblooded do have numerous charms that specify how they work underwater. Okay, mostly it is that they ignore penalties, but a few have bonus effects.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T01:21:47-07:00","id":1219897,"title":"","content":"Given that naval combat is a fairly developed thing in this ruleset and that we have water themed exalts, I find it surprising that neither book so far had much in the way of swimming charms. I suppose athletics excellencies and some of the resistance charms cover the bases?<br /> <br /> Yes, swimming charms would be situational, but so are sail charms, are they not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:23:00-07:00","id":1220013,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, I suppose most of the \u201cgotta go fast\u201d Charms are probably also compatible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T12:24:53-07:00","id":1220057,"title":"","content":"It's certainly my assumption that <i>Lightning Speed</i> enhances swimming the same way it does running (and rushes making use of either sort of movement). And I'd think that <i>Foe-Vaulting Leap</i> could be used to outmaneuver one's opponent in three dimensions underwater.<br /> <br /> Sail charms seem to be mostly situational to captaining your own ship, just as Survival charms are mostly situational to having a trained pet/familiar that you want to enhance. Not that <i>Salty Dog Method</i> isn't a neat charm, but I'd have liked the charmset to go into a little more depth for things you can do at sea even if you don't own the boat you're on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 05-18-2018, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T17:51:41-07:00","id":1220141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1219522-swimming-and-underwater-rules?p=1220057#post1220057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's certainly my assumption that <i>Lightning Speed</i> enhances swimming the same way it does running (and rushes making use of either sort of movement). And I'd think that <i>Foe-Vaulting Leap</i> could be used to outmaneuver one's opponent in three dimensions underwater.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise, I think Monkey Leap Technique allows you to leap out of the water like a dolphin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T22:55:43-07:00","id":1220187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1219522-swimming-and-underwater-rules?p=1220141#post1220141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Likewise, I think Monkey Leap Technique allows you to leap out of the water like a dolphin.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the creative thinking which I think the devs were relying upon by not having explicit swimming &quot;rules&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11847-kfinigan","name":"KFinigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T02:56:57-07:00","id":1220214,"title":"","content":"While we're on the subject, Soaring Leap Technique is an Air-aspected Terrestrial Athletics Charm which supplements Rushes and Disengages, but is clearly NOT intended to work underwater.<br /> <br /> It's meant to be expressed as a leap into the air, using the assistance of air. So like Monkey Leap Technique, it could be used when treading or breaking the water's surface, but not while swimming under it, even if they mechanically do very different things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T03:33:37-07:00","id":1220220,"title":"","content":"We need a water-aspect athletics charm that facilitates leaping like a dolphin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T05:18:24-07:00","id":1220230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1219522-swimming-and-underwater-rules?p=1220220#post1220220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need a water-aspect athletics charm that facilitates leaping like a dolphin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just said that Soaring Leap Technique could do that, and Dragon Surmounts The Waterfall easily could as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}